# Backend environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` to use it. This file did not exist before issue #34, so
# DATABASE_URL was previously documented only in prose in README.md and
# docs/backend-setup-spec.md.
#
# PRECEDENCE, highest first:
#   1. the process environment
#   2. `<CWD>/.env`      <- discovery is CWD-RELATIVE
#   3. the defaults below
#
# Note step 2: pydantic-settings resolves `env_file=".env"` against the
# *current working directory*, not the repository root. Launching the backend
# from `backend/` therefore ignores a repo-root `.env`. Changing that discovery
# rule is deliberately out of scope for issue #34 - it would alter behaviour for
# anyone relying on a CWD-local `.env`. See README.md "Which database am I
# using?".

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Unset by default means: an ABSOLUTE path under the repository root,
#   <repo-root>/data/scientific_home_cluster.db
# which is identical from every working directory. The directory is created
# lazily, on first connect - importing the package creates nothing.
#
# Set this to point at a database elsewhere (e.g. a Syncthing volume). An
# absolute path is strongly preferred: a relative one is resolved against the
# working directory, so two launch directories mean two different databases.
# A relative value still works and is only warned about, never rejected.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////absolute/path/to/scientific_home_cluster.db
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./relative.db

# --- Local server state -------------------------------------------------
#
# Holds the generated JWT signing key, so tokens survive a restart. Unset means
# <repo-root>/.shc (absolute, CWD-independent). Previously the default was the
# literal ".shc", so the key was written into whatever directory the process
# was launched from.
# SHC_STATE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/.shc

# --- Demo data ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# false (default): a fresh database starts empty, and metrics/logs are never
# invented on read. true: seeds the 10 demo jobs / 4 demo nodes on first use.
# SEED_DEMO_DATA=true